{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"subscript"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"orKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"key","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Key","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"key","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key to use to get a value"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In fact if it seems some rules are missing, or weight are not managed, if the font family only is returned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user has an higher probability to use the expected font. Because if a mashup of family name and weight is returned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it can produce a PostScript identifier not available, so not usable, so implying a fallback to default system font like "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"San Francisco"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Because PostScript identifiers in most of cases do not have whitespaces, remove them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["    \/\/ Given a dictionary with one value","    let myDict: PostScriptFontNamesMap = [PSFNMK(\"Arial\", Font.Weight.bold): \"Aria-BoldMT\"]","","    \/\/ The given value is returned if the key exists","    let keyExists = myDict[PSFNMK(\"Arial\", Font.Weight.bold)] \/\/ Arial-BoldMT","","    \/\/ But if the key does not exist, the only the key is returned","    let keyDoesNotExist = myDict[PSFNMK(\"Luciole\", Font.Weight.bold)] \/\/ Luciole"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSFoundations\/documentation\/OUDSFoundations","doc:\/\/OUDSFoundations\/documentation\/OUDSFoundations\/Swift","doc:\/\/OUDSFoundations\/documentation\/OUDSFoundations\/Swift\/Dictionary"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"subscript","fragments":[{"text":"subscript","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"orKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" _: ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Key","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Subscript","role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Key","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostScriptFontNamesMapKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Value","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"modules":[{"name":"Foundations","relatedModules":["Swift"]}],"title":"subscript(orKey:)","externalID":"s:SD15OUDSFoundationsAA25PostScriptFontNamesMapKeyVRszSSRs_rlE02orG0SSAC_tcip","extendedModule":"Swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/oudsfoundations\/swift\/dictionary\/subscript(orkey:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSFoundations\/documentation\/OUDSFoundations\/Swift\/Dictionary\/subscript(orKey:)"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If there is no value for the given "},{"code":"key","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", returns the description of this key,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"i.e.font family name without the font weight in the end and without whitespaces.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"ic_layer